Added a VLAN Group per Location to the IP Fabric integration, named after the Location, so that Nautobot constrains a VLAN ID to one VLAN there. Nautobot enforces uniqueness on `(vlan_group, vid)` and enforces nothing where a VLAN has no group, so VLANs that predate the group are moved into it on the first sync after upgrading, whether or not anything else about them changed. A VLAN already filed under another group keeps it, and one whose VLAN ID or name is already taken inside the group is left ungrouped and reported. A group that already belongs to another Location is left alone and reported, and selecting VLAN Groups under Strict Objects has the sync match an existing group rather than create one.
